                <mxCell id="legend" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=2;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=12;fillColor=#F8F9FA;strokeColor=#AAB7B8;fontColor=#232F3E;" value="&lt;b style=&#39;font-size:14px&#39;&gt;Flow legend&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;① Load the web UI from S3 static hosting&lt;br&gt;② Sign up / sign in via Cognito Hosted UI &amp;rarr; ID token (JWT)&lt;br&gt;③ REST calls with JWT; API Gateway validates it against the Cognito User Pool, then invokes the API Lambdas&lt;br&gt;④ Browser uploads the file straight to S3 with a presigned PUT URL (duplicate SHA-256 checksums rejected first)&lt;br&gt;⑤ S3 sends Object Created to EventBridge; rule 1 (key prefix uploads/) &amp;rarr; thumbnail Lambda, which writes a resized, compressed copy to thumbnails/ (outside the rule&#39;s prefix, so no re-trigger)&lt;br&gt;⑥ Rule 2 matches the same event &amp;rarr; SQS queue &amp;rarr; tagging Lambda, in parallel (at most 2 at a time; dead-letter queue for repeated failures; videos: one frame every 10 s)&lt;br&gt;⑦ Tagging Lambda gets a Cognito access token as a machine client (OAuth client credentials, scope aussie-ecoguard/infer; reused for its 1-hour life) and calls Cloud Run over HTTPS with it and a presigned GET URL; Cloud Run checks it against the Cognito JWKS of the trusted user pools (AWS &amp;rarr; GCP only, no AWS keys in GCP)&lt;br&gt;⑧ At startup Cloud Run downloads the model version (weights + config.json) named by an environment variable &amp;rarr; new model with no code change&lt;br&gt;⑨ Species counts, file type, file URL and thumbnail URL saved to DynamoDB&lt;br&gt;⑩ DynamoDB Streams &amp;rarr; notify Lambda &amp;rarr; SNS (filter policy per tag) &amp;rarr; subscriber email&lt;br&gt;⑪ Query by file / lost-pet photo: browser sends image + Cognito JWT to Cloud Run, which verifies it with the Cognito JWKS and runs inference in memory (never stored); the returned tags are then searched via ③&lt;br&gt;Chatbot: chat Lambda &amp;rarr; Lex V2 &amp;rarr; fulfillment by the search Lambda&lt;br&gt;Subscriptions: subscribe Lambda creates an SNS email subscription with a per-tag filter policy&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Line styles:&lt;/b&gt; solid = synchronous request &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; dashed = asynchronous event / token validation" vertex="1">
